    "https://www.kenyon.edu/careers-outcomes/the-kenyon-network/": {
      "title": "The Kenyon Network",
      "description": "The Kenyon Network | Kenyon College Skip to main content Kenyon College Home Calls to Action Navigation Apply Visit Menu You are here: Home Careers & Outcomes The Kenyon Network The Kenyon Network A global community of Kenyon mentors will help shape your perspective and future. Explore This Section Close Explore This Section Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Mentorship Matters When you join the Kenyon community, you join a global network of alumni and parent career mentors from more than 200 industries who are eager to get to know you and help connect you with job shadows, resume reviews, internships and interviews. Tap into the Kenyon Network This global network of Kenyon alumni and parent career mentors can offer invaluable insight and support. Complete a job shadow A job shadow is an opportunity for students to explore a career of interest by observing an alumnus, alumna, parent or other volunteer in their place of work, typically for a period of 1-5 days. Try an externship Externships are project-based learning opportunities designed and offered by Kenyon alumni and parents who offer coaching and feedback. Join the Kenyon Network on LinkedIn to connect with professionals in your field of interest. Kenyon Network on LinkedIn The Kenyon Network at Work Setting the Scene Through a job shadow with set decorator Rosemary Brandenburg ’78, a film major experienced the ins and outs of a professional production. Categories Alumni Careers Open Mind in Year One - related video Running time: 2:18 Open Mind in Year One First Person: Student Life at Kenyon In his first year, Hyun Cho '26 explored course topics and career interests with an open mind. Categories Careers Athletics Alumni Finding Her Audience In the News Alumni connections helped Mia Sherin ’22 broaden her horizons as a writer, leading to a budding career in New York City. Categories Alumni Careers Let the Sunshine In Kenyon News Environmental studies major Jayne Gelman ’22 is drawn toward the light of a career in solar energy development. Categories Science Student Life Kenyon alumni believe in giving back. What better way than by sharing their professional passions and know-how? Physics major Christian Solorio ’18 shadows Megan Harvey ’05, a flight controller for the International Space Station. India Amos ’17 shadows James Fleming '91 and Anna Bammerlin ’14 at the U.S. Agency for International Development. John Hays ’82 gives Kristin Toms ’20 and Brady Furlich ’19 an insider’s look at Christie’s, the famous British auction house. Leticia Osei-Bonsu ’17 gets a taste of the food industry with Jeni’s Splendid Ice Creams brand ambassador Elizabeth McLees ’12. A double major in neuroscience and chemistry, Juliette Lowe '25 shadowed Dr. Ashley Karpinos '03, an associate professor at Vanderbilt University Medical Center who specializes in internal medicine and pediatrics sports medicine. Sascha Shapiro ’25 explored what a career in finance might look like when he met with Mac Carroll ’11 at GM Asset Management in New York City as part of a job shadow program organized by the Career Development Office. Kenyon students and alumni connect at a networking event. English and anthropology major Taylor Hazan ’19 shadows Susie Heimbach ’98 at the New York Public Library. Kenyon Address Gambier , Ohio 43022 , USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Navigation Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn tiktok Visiting Kenyon Navigation Directions Campus Map Kenyon Commits To Navigation Mission & Values Accessibility Non-Discrimination Privacy Kenyon Affiliates Brown Family Environmental Center The Gund Kenyon Review Philander Chase Conservancy Footer Navigation Employment Bookstore Emergency Title IX Policies Make a Gift © Copyright 2026 Site Menu Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Search Submit CTAs Navigation Apply Visit Site Navigation Academics Departments and Majors Our Faculty Advising & Resources Experiential Learning Global Learning Student Research Writing at Kenyon Library Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Visit Kenyon Apply to Kenyon Financial Aid & Scholarships Connect with Us Request Information Campus Life Inclusion & Belonging Residential Life Dining on Campus Health & Safety Civic Engagement Sustainability & Green Initiatives Clubs & Organizations Arts & Culture Careers & Outcomes Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Athletics Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Explore Kenyon Navigation in brief in pictures in numbers in our own words in the world on a tour Links For Navigation Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community New Students Close"
    },
    "https://www.kenyon.edu/careers-outcomes/outcomes-report-2025/": {
      "title": "Career Outcomes Report 2025",
      "description": "Outcomes Report 2025 | Kenyon College Skip to main content Kenyon College Home Calls to Action Navigation Apply Visit Menu You are here: Home Careers & Outcomes Outcomes Report 2025 Career Outcomes Report 2025 Explore This Section Close Explore This Section Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Class of 2025: After Graduation Within six months of graduation, 90% of 2025 graduates were employed, continuing their education or committed to other plans. (knowledge rate: 80%*) Employment Industries Sampling of Employers Continuing Education 89% of 2025 graduates who planned to attend graduate or professional school were successful in getting admitted to one of their top three choices. Sampling of Graduate Schools and Programs How Kenyon’s Career Development Office Drives Student Success Students who engage with the Career Development Office achieve better outcomes. Among Class of 2025 graduates, those at Level 3 in the CDO Rewards Program had 100% positive outcomes (working or continuing education) with 0% still seeking employment, compared to 82% positive outcomes for non-participants. Early engagement matters. *Knowledge rate refers to the percentage of graduates for whom information of their first destination career outcomes has been obtained in accordance with the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) standards. The statistics in this report include survey data reported by graduates, LinkedIn profile information and knowledge shared by reliable sources. Kenyon Address Gambier , Ohio 43022 , USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Navigation Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn tiktok Visiting Kenyon Navigation Directions Campus Map Kenyon Commits To Navigation Mission & Values Accessibility Non-Discrimination Privacy Kenyon Affiliates Brown Family Environmental Center The Gund Kenyon Review Philander Chase Conservancy Footer Navigation Employment Bookstore Emergency 